### Local runtime state ###
# The relay's own working directory: per-run event logs, the generated route table, the install
# manifest, the dashboard's port hint and the claims a running relay learned. All regenerable.
/work/
/logs/

# Written next to the jar by the launcher. Both are artifacts: relay-routes.json is extracted from
# the bundled template, and drelay.jar is the build output of build.ps1 or Maven. (The template
# itself lives in src/main/resources/, which these root-anchored rules do not match.)
/relay-routes.json
/drelay.jar
/drelay-*.jar
/drelay-update.log

### Local tool installs and scratch analysis (regenerable, never published) ###
/.tools/
/.dnscan/

### Game binaries and decompiled client source (third-party; not ours to publish) ###
/binaries/
/decomp/
*.dll
*.exe
*.nupkg
*.zip

### Generated research inputs ###
# The full IL dump of the game assembly is an 85 MB artifact regenerated from the installed
# build with ilspycmd; it is third-party content and is never published. The small tools and the
# raw measurement outputs beside it ARE tracked, because they are the evidence behind the reports.
/autododgeresearch/il/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

### Subagent scratch directories ###
# Research agents download reference sources (e.g. JNA jars and sources) into a scratch
# directory. It is regenerable and never published; the distilled findings live in
# autododgeresearch/.
/.research/
### Commit-message scratch ###
/autododgeresearch/.commitmsg
